{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/collections/suffolk-local-government-reorganisation","content_id":"367aefd7-84f2-4b17-8418-1ba093c1c231","description":"Documents relating to the government’s programme of local government reorganisation in Suffolk.","details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><h2 id=\"timeline\">Timeline</h2>\n\n<h4 id=\"february-2025\">5 February 2025</h4>\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/local-government-reorganisation-invitation-to-local-authorities-in-two-tier-areas/letter-suffolk\">invitation letter</a> sent to Suffolk councils set out their milestones for reorganisation.</p>\n\n<p>They were invited to submit final proposals by 26 September 2025.</p>\n\n<h4 id=\"november-2025\">19 November 2025</h4>\n\n<p>A <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://questions-statements.parliament.uk/written-statements/detail/2025-11-19/hcws1071\">written ministerial statement</a> was made to Parliament. This set out that a <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/consultations/local-government-reorganisation-in-norfolk-and-suffolk\">consultation on local government reorganisation in Suffolk</a> was launched.</p>\n\n<p>​For the purposes of the consultation, the proposals in Norfolk and Suffolk have been grouped together.</p>\n\n<p>On the same day, the Minister of State for Local Government and Homelessness, Alison McGovern MP, wrote to the leaders of councils in Suffolk to thank them for their proposals and to inform them of the consultation.</p>\n\n<h4 id=\"march-2025\">25 March 2025</h4>\n\n<p>A <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://questions-statements.parliament.uk/written-statements/detail/2026-03-25/hcws1455\">written ministerial statement</a> was made to Parliament, setting out the Secretary of State’s decision to implement the proposal for 3 unitary councils to be established in Suffolk.</p>\n\n<p>Secondary legislation, which will be subject to Parliamentary approval, will now be taken forward to abolish existing councils, establish new councils and make transitional arrangements. </p>\n\n<p>​Accompanying this announcement, a letter was sent to <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/local-government-reorganisation-decision-letter-to-suffolk-leaders\">Suffolk council leaders</a>.</p>\n\n<h4 id=\"september-2026\">7 September 2026</h4>\n\n<p>On 7 September 2026, the Minister for Local Government, Devolution and Regional Growth wrote to local government reorganisation council leaders.</p>\n\n<p>This letter announced the withdrawal of the current decisions for:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Essex, Southend-on-Sea and Thurrock</li>\n  <li>Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton</li>\n  <li>Norfolk</li>\n  <li>Suffolk</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>It also announced a rapid review of the local government reorganisation programme. This includes decisions taken in July 2026 and the 2 outstanding areas awaiting decisions.</p>\n\n<p>The Secretary of State also announced these measures in an oral statement to Parliament on 7 September 2026.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"Review update letter to council leaders added.","public_timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:08:37Z"},{"note":"Programme review and decisions withdrawal letter to council leaders added.","public_timestamp":"2026-09-07T16:04:31Z"},{"note":"Implementation letter to Suffolk council chief executives added.","public_timestamp":"2026-03-31T09:49:11Z"},{"note":"Decision letter to Suffolk council leaders added.","public_timestamp":"2026-03-25T13:14:48Z"},{"note":"Letter to  council leaders on publicity code added.","public_timestamp":"2025-11-19T16:30:46Z"},{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2025-11-19T00:00:00Z"}],"collection_groups":[{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\">\n</div>","documents":["73190f00-b5a6-4b82-bd71-dd279da6766a"],"title":"Consultations"},{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\">\n</div>","documents":["2d4c8dae-f904-4f01-b20b-5b49dfc9b238","c504c71b-3378-462f-8f9d-a9fc8b5fe09b","b25be8ad-483b-45a4-9849-504ba4